-- title:
--   Theorem 1, p. 2 — for α > 3, k²((Ψ+Φ)(x_k) − min(Ψ+Φ)) → 0 and k‖x_{k+1} − x_k‖ → 0
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal H$ be a real Hilbert space. Let $\Psi:\mathcal H\to\mathbb R\cup\{+\infty\}$ be proper, lower semicontinuous and convex, and let $\Phi:\mathcal H\to\mathbb R$ be convex and continuously differentiable with $L$-Lipschitz continuous gradient. Suppose that $S=\operatorname{argmin}(\Psi+\Phi)\neq\emptyset$. Let $\alpha>3$, $0<s<1/L$, and let $(x_k)$ be generated by the accelerated forward-backward method (2),
--   $$y_k=x_k+\frac{k-1}{k+\alpha-1}(x_k-x_{k-1}),\qquad x_{k+1}=\operatorname{prox}_{s\Psi}\big(y_k-s\nabla\Phi(y_k)\big).$$
--   Then
--   $$\lim_{k\to\infty}k^2\Big((\Psi+\Phi)(x_k)-\min(\Psi+\Phi)\Big)=0\qquad\text{and}\qquad\lim_{k\to\infty}k\,\|x_{k+1}-x_k\|=0 .$$
--   In other words, $(\Psi+\Phi)(x_k)-\min(\Psi+\Phi)=o(k^{-2})$ and $\|x_{k+1}-x_k\|=o(k^{-1})$.
--
--   The classical analysis of Nesterov's method and FISTA gives $O(k^{-2})$ for the function values; this theorem shows that for $\alpha>3$ the rate is strictly faster. By [2, Example 2.13] no rate $O(k^{-p})$ with $p>2$ holds for all $\Phi,\Psi$, so the result is optimal in that sense.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $\Psi$ and $\Psi+\Phi$ take values in the extended reals; $\min(\Psi+\Phi)$ is the infimum $\inf_y(\Psi+\Phi)(y)$, attained by the hypothesis $S\neq\emptyset$. The first limit is taken in the extended reals with real coefficients $k^2$; it is not a real limit of truncated values, so a starting point with $\Psi(x_1)=+\infty$ is allowed and affects only finitely many terms. $0<s<1/L$ is written $sL<1$ with $L\ge0$, so $L=0$ is allowed. $\operatorname{prox}_{s\Psi}$ is a map $P$ with `IsProx s Ψ P`. The run is required to follow (2) from $k=1$ on, with $x_0,x_1$ arbitrary (the coefficient of $x_0$ vanishes at $k=1$).
-- source:
--   Attouch and Peypouquet, The Rate of Convergence of Nesterov's Accelerated Forward-Backward Method is Actually Faster than 1/k^2, arXiv:1510.08740v4, p. 2, Theorem 1 (restated p. 4, Section 1.2)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ThreeOpSplitting_ConvexRates_Problem
import Definitions.Def_NesterovFB_Rates_Algorithm

open Filter Topology InnerProductSpace

namespace NesterovFB.Rates

theorem theorem_1 {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] [CompleteSpace H]
    (Ψ : H → EReal) (Φ : H → ℝ) (L : NNReal) (s α : ℝ) (P : H → H) (x : ℕ → H)
    (hΨ : ThreeOpSplitting.ConvexRates.IsProperClosedConvex Ψ)
    (hΦc : ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ Φ) (hΦd : ContDiff ℝ 1 Φ)
    (hL : LipschitzWith L (gradient Φ))
    (hs : 0 < s) (hsL : s * L < 1)
    (hP : ThreeOpSplitting.ConvexRates.IsProx s Ψ P)
    (hrun : IsAccelFBRun Φ P α s x)
    (hα : 3 < α)
    (hS : ∃ xstar : H, ∀ y, theta Ψ Φ xstar ≤ theta Ψ Φ y) :
    Tendsto (fun k : ℕ => (((k : ℝ) ^ 2 : ℝ) : EReal) * (theta Ψ Φ (x k) - ⨅ y, theta Ψ Φ y))
        atTop (𝓝 0) ∧
      Tendsto (fun k : ℕ => (k : ℝ) * ‖x (k + 1) - x k‖) atTop (𝓝 0) := by sorry

end NesterovFB.Rates
